## Summary
Mayor Bucci of Genoa vents frustration over intercepted comments about pigs causing brawls in the port area and firmly denies allegations that funds from the Morandi bridge were misused for a favor to Spinelli. He demands clarity and expresses readiness to speak with prosecutors regarding the matter.

## Key Points
- Mayor Bucci's intercepted remarks about pigs in the port have ignited controversy and disputes.
- He categorically denies any link between Morandi bridge funds and a favor to Spinelli, labeling it a falsehood.
- Bucci calls for transparency and is prepared to engage with prosecutors to address the issue.


